## 🏗 ARCHITECTURE DECISIONS (why things are the way they are)

### Why 3 projects? (Web, Api, Data)
- **Data** is shared between Web and Api — models + DTOs in one place
- **Api** is standalone — can be deployed separately, has its own config
- **Web** is pure Blazor WASM — no server-side rendering, no DB access

### Why Dapper instead of EF Core?
- Database-First: SQL scripts are the source of truth
- Performance: ~3x faster, no change tracking overhead
- Control: exact SQL, no hidden N+1 queries
- Simplicity: SqlConnectionFactory is 11 lines vs DbContext 400+

### Why Database-First?
- SQL scripts in wwwroot/resources/ define the schema
- ResourceAutoStartService executes them automatically on startup
- Easy versioning: just add a new numbered .sql file
- Resources table tracks execution history per file

### Why JWT instead of session/cookie auth?
- Blazor WASM is a SPA — stateless auth needed
- Token stored in browser LocalStorage
- Refresh token rotation for security
- Roles (Admin, Editor, Viewer) in JWT claims

### Why Bento Grid layout?
- Asymmetric = premium feel, not template-based
- Each box is independent — can be rearranged easily
- Works well on mobile (stacks to single column)
- Responsive without media query hacks

### Why single RAF loop for animations?
- 17 animation modules, but only ONE requestAnimationFrame call
- All scroll handlers feed into one master loop
- No competing RAF calls causing jank
- GPU transforms only (scaleX, translateY, rotateX/Y)
- Mobile: fewer modules active (no parallax/pin/glow)

