## 🔑 CODING CONVENTIONS (follow these exactly)

### C# Controllers
```csharp
// EVERY method follows this pattern:
[HttpGet("endpoint")]
public async Task<IActionResult> GetSomething() {
    try {
        using var c = _db.Create();  // SqlConnectionFactory
        var data = await c.QueryAsync<Model>("SELECT * FROM Table WHERE...");
        return Ok(ApiResponse<List<Model>>.Ok(data.ToList()));
    } catch (Exception ex) {
        await _err.LogAsync(ex, "Controller.Method");  // always log
        return StatusCode(500, ApiResponse<object>.Fail("Friendly message."));
    }
}

// For INSERT with identity:
var id = await c.QuerySingleAsync<int>(
    "INSERT INTO Table (...) OUTPUT INSERTED.Id VALUES (...)", model);

// NEVER: string concatenation for SQL
// ALWAYS: parameterized queries with anonymous objects
```

### Blazor Pages
```razor
@page "/route"
@layout MainLayout
@attribute [Authorize(Roles = "Admin,Editor")]  // if admin page
@inject SomeService Service

@* Every page has loading state *@
@if (!loaded) { <p style="color:#9a9a9a;">Loading...</p> }
else { /* content */ }

@code {
    private bool loaded;
    protected override async Task OnInitializedAsync() {
        try { /* load data */ } catch { /* graceful fallback */ }
        loaded = true;
    }
}
```

### JavaScript
```javascript
// All animations in animations.js
// Single RAF loop: function onScroll() → tick()
// GPU transforms only: scaleX(), translateY(), rotateX/Y()
// NEVER: width, height, top, left for animation
// Passive listeners: { passive: true }
// IntersectionObserver for reveal triggers
// Check reduced motion: window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)')
```

### CSS
```css
/* Mobile-first: base styles = mobile, @media (min-width) = desktop */
/* Use CSS variables from :root */
/* Breakpoints: 481, 769, 1025 */
/* GPU compositing: transform: translateZ(0); backface-visibility: hidden; */
/* Touch: touch-action: manipulation; */
```

