## 🌐 BILINGUAL SYSTEM (English / Persian)

### How it works
- **Translation files**: `wwwroot/lang/en.json` + `wwwroot/lang/fa.json` (9 sections each)
- **JS engine**: `wwwroot/js/lang.js` (170 lines) — loads JSON, rewrites DOM
- **Language switch**: button in hero header (`فا` / `EN`)
- **Persistence**: `localStorage.getItem('lang')` — survives page reload
- **RTL**: `html.rtl` class + CSS overrides for Persian

### Adding to any element
```html
<span data-i18n="hero.line1">Default EN text</span>
<input data-i18n-placeholder="contact.form_name_placeholder" placeholder="Your Name">
```

### Key translations file structure
```
en.json: site, nav, hero, work, about, skills, contact, admin, toasts
fa.json: same structure, Persian values
```

### RTL CSS
- `html.rtl` class applied by lang.js when `direction: "rtl"` in JSON
- RTL rules in main styles.css (29 rules)
- Font switches to Vazirmatn for Persian

### Language files location
```
wwwroot/lang/
├── en.json    (English — 9 sections, 4.5KB)
└── fa.json    (Persian — 9 sections, 5.8KB)
```

---

## 🌐 BILINGUAL SYSTEM (TranslationService — T pattern)

### Architecture
- **Service**: `TranslationService` (scoped) — registered in Program.cs via DI
- **Pattern**: `@inject TranslationService T` → `@T["nav.work"]`
- **JSON files**: `wwwroot/lang/en.json` + `wwwroot/lang/fa.json` (85 keys each)
- **Reactivity**: `T.OnChange` event → components call `InvokeAsync(StateHasChanged)` — no page reload
- **Persistence**: `Blazored.LocalStorage` — language survives refresh
- **RTL**: `T.IsRtl` + `T.Direction` → applied to wrapper div `style="direction:@T.Direction"`
- **Font**: `T.FontFamily` → Vazirmatn for Persian, Inter for English

### How to add text in any Blazor page
```razor
@inject TranslationService T
@implements IDisposable

<span>@T["section.key"]</span>

@code {
    protected override void OnInitialized() => T.OnChange += Refresh;
    private void Refresh() => InvokeAsync(StateHasChanged);
    public void Dispose() => T.OnChange -= Refresh;
}
```

### Adding new translation keys
1. Add key to `wwwroot/lang/en.json` (English value)
2. Add same key to `wwwroot/lang/fa.json` (Persian value)
3. Use `@T["section.key"]` in Blazor or `data-i18n="section.key"` in static HTML
4. JSON structure: nested objects → `T["parent.child"]` (e.g., `T["nav.work"]`)

### Components updated with T service
- `MainLayout.razor` — direction, font, admin sidebar labels, LangSwitcher
- `Index.razor` — all hero, nav, work, about, skills, contact, footer text
- `LangSwitcher.razor` — standalone language toggle button
- `Login.razor` / `Register.razor` — site name in title
- `Admin/Dashboard.razor` — stats labels via API data (not hardcoded)

### Static HTML preview
- `wwwroot/index.html` uses `data-i18n` attributes + `wwwroot/js/lang.js`
- lang.js loads JSON → rewrites DOM → handles RTL + font switching
- Language switcher button auto-injected into hero header

